    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112-a1">

                <pb facs="0143" n="69" xml:id="pg69"/>

                <head>Mr. Jackson to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Office United States Telegraph</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">War Department</hi>.</placeName></opener>
                <p>The following telegram received at Washington, 12 m., February 7, 1865, from
                    Halifax, February 6, 1865:</p>
                <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> H <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Seward</hi>:</p>
                <p>Another raid into the United States from Canada is in contemplation; full
                    particulars and instructions respecting which are given in several letters
                    addressed to N. B. Davis, at Montreal and Toronto.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. M. JACKSON, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
